From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Allow what is shared to be chosen again

What was shared last time is shared again without asking, because the answer
is kept and handed back on the next cast. That is right most of the time and
wrong whenever it is not, and there was no way to say so.

Asking to choose afresh is not a matter of telling the desktop to forget. It
is a matter of not handing back what is held: with nothing to match against,
the desktop asks. What is chosen then comes back as a new answer and is
written down in place of the old one, so the cast after reuses what was just
picked. Saying instead that the session may not be remembered would also get
the question asked, and would leave nothing behind to answer with, which
turns the reuse off rather than stepping past it once.

It has to be known before a session is made, which happens while the helper
is being constructed, before it has been given the address it was started
for. So it is read from the environment, which is available then, rather than
from the address, which is not.

diff -ruN a/src/stream/nd-stream.c b/src/stream/nd-stream.c
--- a/src/stream/nd-stream.c
+++ b/src/stream/nd-stream.c
@@ -798,7 +798,27 @@
       return;
     }
 
-  g_autofree gchar *restore_token = nd_stream_load_restore_token ();
+  /* What was shared last time is shared again without asking, because the
+   * answer is kept and handed back. Asking to choose afresh is therefore not
+   * a matter of telling the desktop to forget: it is a matter of not handing
+   * back what we hold. The desktop then has nothing to match and asks.
+   *
+   * What is kept is still kept. Whatever is chosen this time comes back as a
+   * new answer and is written down in place of the old one, so the next cast
+   * reuses what was just picked. Saying instead that this session may not be
+   * remembered would get the question asked and leave nothing behind to
+   * answer with, which is a way of turning the reuse off rather than a way
+   * past it, and would ask again every time after.
+   *
+   * It has to be known before a session is made, which is while this is being
+   * constructed, before the address this was started for has arrived. The
+   * environment is read here; the address is not. */
+  gboolean pick_afresh = g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("ND_STREAM_PICK"), "new") == 0;
+
+  g_autofree gchar *restore_token = pick_afresh ? NULL : nd_stream_load_restore_token ();
+
+  if (pick_afresh)
+    g_message ("NdStream: Asked to choose what to share, so what was shared before is not offered back.");
 
   xdp_portal_create_screencast_session (self->portal,
                                         XDP_OUTPUT_MONITOR | XDP_OUTPUT_WINDOW | XDP_OUTPUT_VIRTUAL,
